    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** (78.67) and **James Wood** (74.47) lead the charge as our premier offensive engines. **Corbin Carroll** is a mandatory start, benefiting from a 100% stolen base opportunity rate against a lethargic delivery from Quantrill, while **James Wood** capitalizes on his elite 0.415 xwOBA and the leadoff spot to maximize run-scoring potential. **Mickey Moniak** (74.24) also earns a high-leverage start, largely driven by a massive +14% boost from a favorable dynamic platoon split against Jobe. We are aggressively targeting these high-upside spots to mitigate the risks posed by tougher arms like Burns, though **Josh Naylor** (71.59) remains a strong play despite a negative platoon adjustment, as his massive +19% SP skill advantage against Lopez creates a high floor for power production.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jose Caballero** (46.25) on the bench. While his projection is respectable, he suffered a -13% hit due to a poor dynamic platoon matchup and a disadvantageous #9 spot in the order, ultimately falling short of the efficiency offered by **Zach McKinstry** and our middle infield anchors. We are monitoring **Seiya Suzuki** (67.31) closely; while his profile is stellar, the 5% penalty for wind blowing in at the stadium is a legitimate risk that could dampen his power ceiling. The rest of our depth, including **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Griffin Conine**, **Edwin Arroyo**, and **Cole Young**, remains on notice, as does **Giancarlo Stanton**, who remains unavailable due to his status on the IL. We are positioning for maximum contact and SB efficiency, leaning on the data to navigate the mid-September fatigue.",
